--- brief: delivery contract + forge tool rule + draft readback:
3. Use glab-axi for GitLab operations, gh-axi for GitHub operations, and chrome-devtools-axi for browser operations.
Delivery contract: mode=direct-PR forge=gitlab
When it is implemented and committed, push your branch and open a merge request with `glab-axi` that is ready for review, not a draft.
Before you report done, read the merge request back from the forge and confirm it is not a draft (`glab-axi mr view <iid> --full` must print `draft: no`, where <iid> is the merge request number from your MR URL); if it is a draft, mark it ready with `glab-axi mr update <iid> --ready`.
A draft cannot be merged, so a done report on one leaves the merge unasked.
If you deliberately keep the PR a draft, append `paused [at=<epoch>]: {why the draft is held}` instead of done.

